# Gitignored local files copied into each new worktree (.gitignore syntax).
# Only paths that match here AND are gitignored get copied; tracked files never are.
# Honored by Claude Code (--worktree, subagent worktrees, desktop parallel sessions)
# and Codex managed worktrees; not by `git worktree add` or a WorktreeCreate hook.
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees#copy-gitignored-files-into-worktrees
# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/environments/git-worktrees

# Holds the real chat ids CLAUDE.md's "Write targets" limits writes to; without it
# the @import breaks and e2e/manual sends in the worktree have no allowed target.
/CLAUDE.local.md

# `just run` and `./larkim --config ./dev.yaml` read it. data_dir is under ~, so
# every worktree shares one dev database instead of cold-syncing its own.
/dev.yaml

# Deliberately not copied:
# - .claude/settings.local.json: permission approvals are stored in and read from
#   the main checkout for every worktree; a copy would be a second source of truth.
